add(13,img('ambiguity.png','Two real digits; illustrative overlapping one-coordinate distributions'),[p('Two different digits can have overlapping noisy distributions.'),p('The noisy observation may fit more than one clean image.'),eq(r'p(x_0\mid x_t)\ \text{can retain uncertainty}')], 'This is a schematic of overlapping support, not a claim that two independently sampled arrays are identical. The learned predictor uses the training distribution to estimate missing information.', 'Can removing noise be a unique inverse?','Generally no. Corruption loses information; inference uses a distribution over explanations.')
