add(27,code('t = torch.randint(1, T+1, (B,), device=x0.device)\neps = torch.randn_like(x0)\nab = alpha_bar[t].reshape(B, 1, 1, 1)\nxt = ab.sqrt()*x0 + (1-ab).sqrt()*eps\neps_hat = model(xt, t)\nloss = F.mse_loss(eps_hat, eps)\noptimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\nloss.backward()\noptimizer.step()'),[p('Sample a timestep and the target noise.'),p('Gather each example’s coefficient and reshape it for broadcasting.'),p('Use the forward formula to construct the noisy input.'),p('Predict the noise, compute MSE and update the weights.')], 'The sentinel alpha_bar[0]=1 makes indices agree with mathematical time. Walk the active conceptual code line through the tuple diagram. Boilerplate and a readable named-layer model are in the executable companion.')
