add(41,'<div class="architecture" data-architecture="unet"></div>',[p('Down: 28²×32 → 14²×64 → 7²×128.'),p('The middle residual block also receives the time embedding.'),p('Up: skips concatenate channels; 128→64 and 64→32. 814,145 parameters.')], 'The implemented model uses stride-two convolutions down, nearest resize plus convolution up, additive time embeddings and a linear 1 by 1 head. Concatenated channels must be counted before each decoder block. Exact parameter count is recorded by code.',layout='wide')
add(42,diagram([('t → sin/cos','[B,64] → MLP',A),('Project channels','[B,C,1,1]',T),('Add to features','[B,C,H,W]',B)]),[p('Add the projected time vector at every spatial location.'),p('Repeat this in the encoder, middle and decoder blocks.')], 'A time scalar becomes a useful feature vector through sinusoidal features and learned projections. Normalise after the first one-to-32-channel projection. Group counts divide output channels. The same time path remains active during generation.',layout='wide')
add(43,diagram([('Latent patches','[B,256,16]',B),('Transformer','[B,256,d]',T),('Unpatchify','[B,4,32,32]',B)]),[p('A 4×32×32 latent splits into 256 patches of size 2×2.'),p('Each output token predicts the 16 entries needed to rebuild its patch.')], 'No CLS pooling produces a dense image. Original DiT is class-conditioned with time/class modulation; it is not universally a text cross-attention design. Its learned-variance head has extra channels, unlike this noise-only teaching head.',source=DIT,layout='wide')
add(44,diagram([('Image','[B,3,512,512]',B),('Autoencoder','spatial latent',T),('Latent','[B,4,64,64]',P)]),[p('Consider these shapes from an SD-v1-style system.'),eq(r'512^2/64^2=64\quad\text{spatial positions}'),eq(r'\frac{3\cdot512^2}{4\cdot64^2}=48\quad\text{scalar entries}'),p('Runtime and memory gains need separate measurements.')], 'Use distinct words for positions and scalars. This latent is a spatial tensor, unlike the tiny VAE vector used earlier. Other autoencoders use different shapes. A representation-size ratio alone is not a performance benchmark.',source=LDM,layout='wide')
